quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  7,121,They said: ‘We believe in the Lord of all worlds.
  7,122,(The) Lord of Musa (Moses) and Harun (Aaron).’
  7,123,"Pharaoh said: ‘Have you believed in Him before I permit you? This is indeed a plot you have secretly devised in this city so that you may expel its people from it. Soon, you will know (the consequences)."
  7,124,"Surely, I shall cut off your hands and your feet on alternate sides, and then, most certainly, I shall crucify you all.’"
  7,125,"They said: ‘Indeed, we are to return to our Lord."
  7,126,And you are vindictive towards us only because we have believed in the signs of our Lord when they came to us (clearly).’ ‘Our Lord! Shower upon us patience and grant us to die as Muslims (i.e. those who submit to Allah).’
  7,127,"And the leaders of Pharaoh’s people said: ‘Will you leave Musa (Moses) and his people to cause disorder in the land, and to abandon you and your gods?’ He (Pharaoh) said: ‘We shall slaughter their sons and keep their women alive, and surely we are dominant over them.’"
  7,128,"Musa (Moses) said to his people: ‘Seek help from Allah and be patient. Surely, the earth belongs to Allah, and He gives its inheritance to whomever He wills among His servants. And the final outcome will be in favour of those who are God-conscious.’"
  7,129,"They said: ‘We were persecuted before you came to us and (also) after you came to us.’ He (Moses) said: ‘Perhaps your Lord will destroy your enemy and make you successors in the land, and then He will see how you behave.’"
  7,130,"And indeed, We afflicted the people of Pharaoh with drought and shortage of crops; perhaps they might be mindful (of advice)."
